// Kryspal Media Plugin protocol v1: user sync, e.g. Trakt's watched history and now-playing reports.
//
// Capabilities and the methods they map to:
//   usersync.link                         BeginLink, PollLink, Unlink
//   usersync.scrobble                     Scrobble
//   usersync.watched.pull, watched.push   PullWatched, PushWatched
//
// Plugins are stateless: the host stores members' credentials encrypted and passes them in on every call; when they need
// updating (e.g. refresh token rotation), the plugin returns updated_credentials with the response,
// and the host **writes them before using them**, and guarantees the same credential is never used concurrently. Plugins
// must not store or log credentials, and never see member IDs.
// An invalid credential (revoked, or expired and not refreshable) returns UNAUTHENTICATED: the host only marks this
// member's link as needing to be re-linked; the plugin stays online.

